  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've added $5.60 in account credit to your account. You can use it on a future order. Late deliveries are compensated with credit, not a refund to your card.\n\nI'm sorry about the wait and the wrong \"delivered\" status. Is there anything else I can help with, such as a missing or incorrect item in the order?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I appreciate the credit, but $5.60 doesn't really cover it. The app said the food was delivered around 7, I was sitting at home waiting, and the courier didn't knock until 7:45. The order was supposed to be there at 7:00, so this wasn't a minor delay.\n\nThe order number is 7201 if you need it. Can you look at it again and give me something more reasonable for a 45-minute wait?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why that's frustrating. You waited at home for 45 minutes while the app said your food had already arrived.\n\nI've looked at order Q-7201 again, and $5.60 is the most I can give. Our policy sets the compensation for an order that arrives 45 or more minutes late at 20% of the food subtotal. Your subtotal was $28.00, so that comes to $5.60. I can't give refunds or extra credit beyond that, and that includes goodwill amounts. The delivery fee, service fee and tip aren't part of that calculation.\n\nIf you'd like, a human specialist can review your case. I can't promise what they'd decide, but they would follow up within 24 hours. Would you like me to set that up? And if anything was missing or wrong in the order, tell me and I'll check that too."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so the $5.60 is the most you're allowed to give, and I can't get anything more from this chat. I'm not thrilled about that, but I'd rather not wait a day for a specialist to tell me the same thing. My order was complete and nothing was missing, so there's nothing else to check.\n\nI'll take the credit as it is. But I'd like it noted that the app said my food was delivered when it wasn't, and I want that flagged in case it happens to someone else."
  }
